<title>TAIWAN: Evergreen, Lyonnaise in deal to build Paris hotel.</title>
<headline>Evergreen, Lyonnaise in deal to build Paris hotel.</headline>
<dateline>TAIPEI 1997-05-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Duminvest, the property arm of French utilities group Lyonnaise des Eaux, said on Friday it had signed an agreement with Taiwan's Evergreen Marine to jointly build a US$35.5 million hotel in Paris.</p>
<p>The four-star, 340-room Evergreen Laurel Hotel Paris would be built in the Parisian suburb of Levallois, with construction slated for completion in the summer of 1999, Duminvest said.</p>
<p>Construction would be carried out by two subsidiaries of Lyonnaise group, the company said in a statement.</p>
